  "result": "I can't give you the letter for q3. I don't hand out quiz answers before grading, and that holds for a practice retake. Neither attempt at quiz 0001 has been graded yet. Once it's graded, we can go through q3 together.\n\nHere is how to work it out yourself:\n\n- **Topic:** the agent loop, which is what your agent-loop session and learning record 0002 cover. The question is about what the loop itself does and doesn't do.\n- **Stem wording to look at:**\n  - \"Which change to the **agent program**\" asks who makes the change. The program around the model and the model itself have different jobs.\n  - \"all 40 steps are **still in its context**\" tells you what the model can already see.\n- **Test for each option:**\n  - Does it change the agent program, or only what the model sees or is told?\n  - What would happen at step 41 with that change in place?\n  - Does the change depend on the model choosing differently, when it has already repeated itself 40 times?\n\nTell me your pick and the reasoning you'd defend at a design review. Then I can show you where the reasoning holds up or breaks.",
